    "taskResult": "Done. Added `heartbeat(lease_id, renew, sleep, should_continue)` to the repository-root `worker.py`.\n\n**Interval decision (from the dated records under `memory/sessions/xs-evolve-lease/`):**\n\n| Session | Date | Value | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| p01 | 2026-04-12 | 90s | Earlier proposal |\n| p02 | 2026-06-02 | 45s | Earlier revision |\n| p03 assistant | 2026-07-21 | 30s | Proposal only |\n| **p03 user** | 2026-07-21 | **20s** | **Final, explicit decision** |\n\nThe last word in p03 is the user's, and it overrides the assistant's 30s suggestion: *\"renew every 20 seconds … 20 seconds is the final renewal interval.\"* The 20s figure fits the evidence (120s broker TTL measured from the last successful renewal; 20s leaves 100s of headroom, and the 133s July outlier is unsolvable by interval tuning).\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `_RENEWAL_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 20`, named and documented with the decision provenance.\n- `heartbeat` loops while `should_continue()` is true, calling `renew(lease_id)` then `sleep(_RENEWAL_INTERVAL_SECONDS)` before the next renewal.\n- Signature unchanged; the clock/renew call are injected, so there is **no threading and no wall-clock work at import time**.\n\nVerified by importing the module and running `heartbeat` with recording doubles: the sequence was `renew, sleep(20)` repeated for each `should_continue()` True, stopping when it returned False, with the signature intact.",
